  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Role and Founding
    
    Summit-Lord of Qingfu'spire, the Aurora Stack faction governing the Promenade Ward and its satellite spires. Yahailong founded the Ward during the Frozen Peace, marshaling settlers into a viable colony through command of three magics: Slide Prism, the aurora-harvesting technique she used to move resources across fractured ice; Ice-whisper (shimmer), the dangerous fire-touched aurora magic enabling communion with the deep; and Snowdrift-numb (astral), the ice-memory channeling art discovered by her co-founder Hainou mewei'Frostglass near the Bastion Apex.
    
    Tall even by Aurora Stack standards, Yahailong wears layered white robes over ice-plate armor whose pauldrons have gone unpolished since the Orca Incursion, when three raiders breached the outer wall. She carries an aurora-glass staff that flickers faintly — a detail others note but do not inquire about. Her flippers bear scars from early Slide Prism experiments. The magic still burns her when she overreaches.
    
    ## The Fire-Core Diversion
    
    During the founding's third winter, Yahailong diverted two fire-cores from a scheduled shipment to construct heat-barriers on the western perimeter against orca scouts, replacing them three days later through a private Nightshelf requisition. In the interval, two eastern-quarter families — Moqai and Xuelin — went three nights without heat and froze. Their deaths were recorded on the Promenade memorial among settlers who Walked.
    
    Yahailong then had Hainou teach her Snowdrift-numb and entered the ice at Bastion Apex to reshape its memory of the diversion and the deaths. Years of practice left her flippers with permanent nerve damage — an unnatural stillness past shaking entirely, which reads as composure to those unaware of its cause. She has never returned to the deep tunnels for fire-core trade negotiations. The Nightshelf noticed years ago and stopped commenting.
    
    She refuses to visit the memorial. Instead she walks the Promenade at dawn, checking the crystalline conductors that power the ward's heat-vents.
    
    ## Exposure and Succession
    
    The cover-up was uncovered when Zhinghoua lang'Gleam, an Aurora Stack investigator, identified a two-core discrepancy in founding-era shipment records against the eastern quarter's heat-conductor requirements. Confronted with evidence from shadow-ledgers, Yahailong confessed. Snowdrift-numb does not permit true erasure — both original and revision persist in layers.
    
    Yahailong now faces succession discussions within Qingfu'spire. The casualties cannot be added back to the memorial without acknowledging the ice was altered, and the ice was altered by the colony's founder using the colony's own magic.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771589903323_0", anchor: "recorded on the Promenade memorial among settlers who Walked", text: "They did not Walk. They froze in their quarters because the fire-cores that should have heated them were on the western perimeter. Recording them as Walkers was the first falsification — before the ice was ever touched. The Walking's categorical ambiguity made it the perfect administrative grave: no one investigates a Walking because no one is certain what Walking is. Yahailong understood this. The ice-memory alteration came second, to make the reclassification hold under scrutiny. Two layers of revision, and I wrote through both in a single clause.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771589903323_1", anchor: "two eastern-quarter families — Moqai and Xuelin", text: "I corrected myself once already — on the Snowdrift-numb entry — for writing \"two families\" when I meant seven penguins. Here I've done it again. Founding-era residential registers survive in administrative ice. I could have counted. I chose the families' names over their members' names, and I know why: because Yahailong did too.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771589903323_2", anchor: "The Nightshelf noticed years ago and stopped commenting", text: "They processed the private requisition that replaced the cores three days later. They had equivalent records years before Zhinghoua thought to look. Their silence was not courtesy. It was leverage held in reserve.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
